<div class="mb-8">
  <Heading size="2xl" as="h1" class="mb-2">Select</Heading>
  <Text size="lg" tone="subdued" as="h2">
    A form field for choosing a single value from a list of options, built on top of
    Dropdown and Menu for consistent styling and keyboard navigation.
  </Text>
</div>

<!-- Canonical example -->
<div class="mb-8">
  <Example source={'
    <div class="max-w-sm w-full">
      <Select
        name="country"
        label="Country"
        placeholder="Select a country..."
        options={[
          {label: "United States", value: "us"},
          {label: "Canada", value: "ca"},
          {label: "United Kingdom", value: "uk"}
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  '}/>
</div>

<!-- Usage -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Usage</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg bg-card overflow-hidden">
    <CodeBlock code={"<Select\n  name=\"country\"\n  label=\"Country\"\n  placeholder=\"Select a country...\"\n  options={[\n    {label: \"United States\", value: \"us\"},\n    {label: \"Canada\", value: \"ca\"},\n    {label: \"United Kingdom\", value: \"uk\"}\n  ]}\n/>"}/>
  </div>
  <Prose class="mt-4">
    <p>
      Select renders a labeled trigger button that opens a floating menu of options. When the user
      picks an option, its value is written to a hidden <code>&lt;input&gt;</code> field so it
      submits with the form. Pass <code>options</code> as an array of <code>{label, value}</code>
      hashes and <code>name</code> for the form field name.
    </p>
  </Prose>
  <div class="border rounded-lg bg-muted/50 overflow-hidden mt-4">
    <CodeBlock code={"Select\n├── Label          (from label prop)\n├── Dropdown\n│   ├── Trigger    (styled button with chevron)\n│   └── Menu       (floating option list)\n├── Hidden input   (carries the selected value)\n└── Help / Error   (optional feedback text)"}/>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- When to Use -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">When to Use</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      Use Select for form fields where the user must choose exactly one value from a predefined
      list. It replaces the native <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> element with a styled, consistent
      alternative that matches the rest of the Orbital design system.
    </p>
    <p>
      For action menus (edit, delete, share) use a <a href="/components/dropdown">Dropdown</a>
      with a <a href="/components/menu">Menu</a> instead — those represent commands, not form
      values. For free-text input with optional suggestions, use a
      <a href="/components/text-field">TextField</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you have fewer than three options and they're all visible at once, consider using radio
      buttons or a segmented control for faster scanning.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Behaviour -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Behaviour</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      Clicking the trigger opens a floating menu positioned below by default. The currently selected
      option is highlighted. Selecting an option closes the menu, updates the trigger label, and
      writes the value to the hidden input. Clicking outside or pressing Escape closes the menu
      without changing the value.
    </p>
    <p>
      The dropdown uses the same Popover/Floating UI system as other Orbital floating components,
      so it automatically flips when near viewport edges. Set <code>position="n"</code> to open
      upward instead.
    </p>
    <p>
      The hidden input participates in standard HTML form submission — no JavaScript needed on the
      server side. Use <code>name</code> to set the form parameter key and <code>selected</code>
      to set an initial value.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Examples -->
<div class="flex flex-col gap-12 mb-12">
  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Pre-selected Value</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Use the <code>selected</code> prop to set an initial value. The trigger label updates
        to show the matching option's label text.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="max-w-sm w-full">
        <Select
          name="language"
          label="Preferred Language"
          selected="en"
          options={[
            {label: "English", value: "en"},
            {label: "Spanish", value: "es"},
            {label: "French", value: "fr"},
            {label: "German", value: "de"},
            {label: "Italian", value: "it"}
          ]}
        />
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">With Disabled Options</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Individual options can be disabled by adding <code>disabled: true</code> to the option
        hash. Disabled options are visible but not selectable.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="max-w-sm w-full">
        <Select
          name="plan"
          label="Subscription Plan"
          placeholder="Choose a plan..."
          help="Some plans are currently unavailable"
          options={[
            {label: "Free Plan", value: "free"},
            {label: "Pro Plan", value: "pro"},
            {label: "Enterprise Plan", value: "enterprise", disabled: true},
            {label: "Team Plan", value: "team"},
            {label: "Ultimate Plan", value: "ultimate", disabled: true}
          ]}
        />
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Error State</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Pass an <code>error</code> string to display validation feedback. The trigger border
        turns red and the error message appears below the field, replacing any help text.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="max-w-sm w-full">
        <Select
          name="category"
          label="Category"
          placeholder="Select a category..."
          error="Please select a category to continue"
          options={[
            {label: "Technology", value: "tech"},
            {label: "Business", value: "business"},
            {label: "Science", value: "science"},
            {label: "Arts", value: "arts"}
          ]}
        />
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Full Width</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Set <code>fullwidth</code> to expand the select to fill its container. The dropdown
        menu matches the trigger width.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <Select
        name="timezone"
        label="Time Zone"
        placeholder="Select your timezone..."
        fullwidth
        options={[
          {label: "Pacific Time (PT)", value: "pt"},
          {label: "Mountain Time (MT)", value: "mt"},
          {label: "Central Time (CT)", value: "ct"},
          {label: "Eastern Time (ET)", value: "et"},
          {label: "Greenwich Mean Time (GMT)", value: "gmt"}
        ]}
      />
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Position</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>The dropdown opens below by default. Set <code>position="n"</code> to open upward —
        useful when the select is near the bottom of the viewport.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 w-full max-w-lg">
        <Select
          name="position_top"
          label="Open Upwards"
          placeholder="Select..."
          position="n"
          options={[
            {label: "Option 1", value: "1"},
            {label: "Option 2", value: "2"},
            {label: "Option 3", value: "3"}
          ]}
        />
        <Select
          name="position_bottom"
          label="Open Downwards"
          placeholder="Select..."
          position="s"
          options={[
            {label: "Option 1", value: "1"},
            {label: "Option 2", value: "2"},
            {label: "Option 3", value: "3"}
          ]}
        />
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Disabled</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Set <code>disabled</code> to prevent interaction entirely. The trigger is visually
        muted and does not respond to clicks.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="max-w-sm w-full">
        <Select
          name="disabled_select"
          label="Unavailable Option"
          placeholder="Cannot select..."
          disabled
          help="This select is currently disabled"
          options={[
            {label: "Option 1", value: "1"},
            {label: "Option 2", value: "2"}
          ]}
        />
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Best Practices -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Best Practices</Heading>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-green-500/30 bg-green-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-green-600">Do</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Always provide a visible label — use <code>labelHidden</code> only when a nearby heading makes the purpose obvious.</li>
          <li>Use descriptive placeholder text that hints at what to choose.</li>
          <li>Include <code>help</code> text when the choice has implications the user should understand.</li>
          <li>Set <code>fullwidth</code> in form layouts where all fields span the full width.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-red-600">Don't</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Use Select for actions — use a Dropdown with a Menu instead.</li>
          <li>Put more than 15-20 options in a Select — consider a searchable autocomplete.</li>
          <li>Disable most options in the list — rethink the available choices.</li>
          <li>Omit the <code>name</code> prop — without it the value won't submit with the form.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- API Reference -->
<div>
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">API Reference</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Prop</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Type</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Values</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Default</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y">
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">options</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Array</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">[{label:, value:, disabled:}]</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">[]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">selected</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Value of the selected option</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">placeholder</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any string</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">"Select..."</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">name</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Form field name</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">id</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any unique string</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">auto-generated</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">label</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any string</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">labelHidden</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Boolean</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">true, false</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">false</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">help</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any string</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">error</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any string</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">disabled</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Boolean</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">true, false</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">false</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">required</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Boolean</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">true, false</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">false</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">position</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Symbol</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">auto, n, ne, e, se, s, sw, w, nw</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">s</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">fullwidth</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Boolean</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">true, false</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">false</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
